  "notes": "Real code, see corpus/ts-sdk-real-slice/PROVENANCE.md. Truth was written by reading each file against docs/SDK_USAGES.md, not from engine output. Calls rooted at a non-client SDK export (zodResponseFormat, recordAudio, the two bedrock helpers bound by destructured dynamic import() of openai/providers/bedrock and openai/providers/bedrock/aws, betaRefusalFallbackMiddleware, new BetaFallbackState()) are recorded with routing unknown and no gap; betaRefusalFallbackMiddleware's positional array literal holds an object whose top-level model key is captured as `model`. Calls on what a request returns (.on(...) chained on a .stream(...) call, stream.finalMessage(), runner.finalResponse(), result.response.text(), message.content.find(...)) are not records. openai/chat.ts builds its baseURL from a template literal over requireEnv(...), a same-file function, so the client is unknown with a base_url_unresolved gap at each call (not base_url_env: no process.env lookup is written in the expression) and the deployment model is a function_call gap. openai/runtime-chat.ts passes `request`, a same-file object literal that is only passed to requests and spread, whose shorthand model is `process.env['BEDROCK_MODEL'] ?? ...`: both calls capture the fallback as env_default and keep env_var; new OpenAI({ provider }) routes unknown with no gap, as in py-sdk-real-slice. Every GoogleGenAI with vertexai: true (with project/location or with an apiKey) routes unknown and every call on it or on its chat, sendMessage and the non-request getHistory included, has an endpoint_option gap; vertexai: false stays google_genai. Gaps sit at calls, never at constructions. The Gemini samples import MODEL_FLASH_LITE and MODEL_EMBEDDING from ./constants.js, which is not in the fixture, so their values are unknowable and only the imported_name gap is recorded (no known_missing entry). A chat's or legacy model's own calls carry no model value or model gap: the model belongs to the chats.create / get